  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see whether payroll verification phishing messages were caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5) heard about an email asking staff to \"verify payroll login\" and asked whether it's legit. She does not mention clicking anything or entering credentials (follow-up question sent to confirm). Checked: her quarantine. Found: Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital \"I\" in place of \"l\"), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 09:09 UTC, marked phishing and not releasable. It was caught for her. She says she \"heard\" about it going around, so others may have received it too and some copies may have reached inboxes. Needed: security review of the sender/domain, block it org-wide, check other mailboxes for delivered copies, and possibly send a company-wide warning. If she says she clicked or entered credentials, switch to KB-029 (P1).",
  "reason": "KB-008: reported suspicious email always escalates; possible multi-user campaign with a lookalike domain"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking with us first. That email is not real. It's a phishing scam. It comes from an address made to look like ours ('brightIine-help', with a capital I in place of the l). Our mail filter caught the copy sent to you, so it never reached your inbox. This won't affect your payroll. Please don't click any links in it, reply to it, or forward it, and if a copy turns up in your inbox, leave it there for now so our security team can look at it. I've sent it to the security team so they can block the sender for everyone. One quick question: did you click a link in a message like this or type your password anywhere? If so, please reply right away so we can secure your account.",
  "internal_note": "KB-008 followed. Account is active and normal. Her quarantine has Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example, 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-09 09:09 UTC, marked phishing and not releasable. Nothing was released. The user doesn't say she interacted with it, but I asked her to confirm. If she clicked or entered credentials, handle as P1 under KB-029. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation 1) to block the sender org-wide. This may be a wider campaign because she 'heard' it's going around.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
